---
---

<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8"/>
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg"/>
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico"/>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover, user-scalable=no"/>
    <meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes"/>
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes"/>
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="black-translucent"/>
    <title>BongBong!</title>
    <style lang="scss">
      $font-size: 10pt;
      $font-color: #c6c6c6;

      html, body {
        margin: 0;
        min-height: 100%;
        background-color: #151515;
        color: $font-color;
        font-family: sans-serif;
        font-size: $font-size;
      }

      a {
        color: #888;
      }

      .wrapper {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: center;
        width: 100%;
        min-height: 100vh;
        /* `viewport-fit=cover` lays the page out under a phone's notch and
           home indicator; the column keeps out of both, so the stage, and
           the HUD and touch controls the game draws in it, never sit
           under them. */
        box-sizing: border-box;
        padding: env(safe-area-inset-top) env(safe-area-inset-right) 0 env(safe-area-inset-left);

        .game, .footer {
          display: flex;
          flex-direction: column;
          align-items: center;
          width: 100%;
        }

        .game {
          position: relative;
          /* The strip kept under the stage for the key hints, on a screen
             tall enough to spare it; a phone on its side gives the stage
             every pixel, its hints being for keyboards anyway. */
          --hints: 72px;

          @media (max-height: 540px) {
            --hints: 0px;
          }

          /* The canvas's box, and the one box the overlay controls and the
             loading panel are positioned in, so they sit on the canvas's
             own edges wherever it lands. It takes the space it is given
             at any shape - the column's width and the viewport's height
             less the hints, here; the whole viewport inside the safe area
             in immersive mode and full screen - and the game fills
             whatever that is: its window follows the box
             (src/app/web.rs), a followed map is framed to it and an
             arena's margins are drawn as ground. */
          .stage {
            position: relative;
            flex: none;
            width: 100%;
            height: calc(100vh - var(--hints) - env(safe-area-inset-top) - env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
            /* The viewport as it is on screen now, a phone's browser bars
               shown or collapsed. */
            height: calc(100dvh - var(--hints) - env(safe-area-inset-top) - env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
          }

          /* The two overlay controls sit together in one row, Full screen
             first, the subscribe link beside it. With a mouse they keep to
             the canvas's *bottom-left* corner, away from the HUD's corner
             clusters along its top (src/hud.rs `corners`). Wherever they
             are, overlay.ts tells the game, which keeps its off-screen
             arrows off them. */
          .overlay-controls {
            position: absolute;
            left: 10px;
            bottom: 10px;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 8px;
            z-index: 2;
            white-space: nowrap;
          }

          /* On a touch screen the bottom corners are the thumbs': the left
             half of the canvas steers wherever a thumb lands and the right
             half fires (src/touch.rs), and the thumbs rest about 22 mm in
             and 18 mm up from those corners (`indicators::thumb_rests`).
             The top corners are the HUD's clusters, and between them there
             is too little room for two labels on a narrow phone - 74
             points, 69 CSS pixels on an iPhone SE. So the controls take a
             band of their own along the top, centred, and the game lays
             its chrome out below it as it does below a safe area: the
             clusters, the panels and the builder's bar all stand clear of
             it, and the world shows on either side. Above the turn card,
             so the way out of immersive mode is always there. */
          @media (hover: none) and (pointer: coarse) {
            .overlay-controls {
              top: 3px;
              bottom: auto;
              left: 50%;
              transform: translateX(-50%);
              z-index: 4;
            }
          }

          .subscribe-link {
            padding: 3px 8px;
            border-radius: 3px;
            background: rgba(46, 46, 46, 0.75);
            color: #ddd;
            text-decoration: none;
            font-size: $font-size;

            &:hover, &:focus-visible {
              color: #fff;
              background: rgba(46, 46, 46, 0.95);
              text-decoration: underline;
            }
          }

          /* Covers exactly the canvas's own box, the stage, so the panel
             is the picture that has not arrived yet rather than a banner
             above it. */
          .loading {
            position: absolute;
            inset: 0;
            z-index: 2;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            gap: 10px;
            background: #1b2118;
            color: #cfe0c4;
            font-size: $font-size;
            text-align: center;
            /* Faded out rather than cut, so a fast connection does not
               produce a one-frame flash of panel. */
            transition: opacity 260ms ease;

            &[hidden] {
              display: none !important;
            }

            &.done {
              opacity: 0;
              pointer-events: none;
            }
          }

          .loading-title {
            margin: 0;
            font-size: calc($font-size * 1.6);
            letter-spacing: 0.08em;
          }

          .loading-track {
            width: min(240px, 50%);
            height: 6px;
            border-radius: 3px;
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
            overflow: hidden;
          }

          /* Width is set by the loader once Emscripten reports byte counts;
             until then it runs an indeterminate sweep, because a bar frozen
             at 0% reads as stalled. */
          .loading-bar {
            width: 30%;
            height: 100%;
            border-radius: 3px;
            background: #8fd07a;
            animation: loading-sweep 1.4s ease-in-out infinite;
          }

          .loading-bar.measured {
            animation: none;
            transition: width 200ms ease;
          }

          .loading-note {
            margin: 0;
            opacity: 0.7;
          }

          @keyframes loading-sweep {
            0% {
              margin-left: -30%;
            }
            100% {
              margin-left: 100%;
            }
          }

          @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
            .loading {
              transition: none;
            }
            .loading-bar {
              animation: none;
            }
          }

          /* A phone held upright. The game is landscape: its chrome is laid
             out for at least 720 x 352 points, its touch stick and trigger
             take the two halves of a wide screen, and a followed map is
             framed no narrower than 4:3 - so in a stage 393 points wide the
             field would be a band a third of the screen tall with tanks two
             millimetres across. The card asks for the phone to be turned
             and covers only the stage; the round runs on behind it and the
             window keeps following the box, so turning the phone shows the
             game at once. A tablet held upright is wide enough to play and
             a desktop window is the player's to size: neither gets it. */
          .turn {
            display: none;
          }

          @media (orientation: portrait) and (max-width: 719.98px) and (hover: none) and (pointer: coarse) {
            .turn {
              position: absolute;
              inset: 0;
              z-index: 3;
              display: flex;
              flex-direction: column;
              align-items: center;
              justify-content: center;
              gap: 14px;
              margin: 0;
              padding: 0 24px;
              /* The page's own background and its light text, so the card
                 reads as the page rather than a coloured panel. */
              background: #151515;
              color: #ddd;
              font-size: calc($font-size * 1.4);
              text-align: center;
            }

            /* A phone on its side, drawn rather than an emoji, so every
               browser shows the same one. */
            .turn::before {
              content: "";
              width: 54px;
              height: 30px;
              border: 3px solid #fff;
              border-radius: 6px;
            }
          }

          canvas {
            display: block;
            /* The canvas fills the stage exactly, and the game makes its
               drawing buffer that box in device pixels (src/app/web.rs),
               so the picture is drawn one buffer pixel to the device pixel
               with nothing left to letterbox. That is also what keeps a
               tap where it lands: raylib maps a touch by dividing by the
               canvas's CSS box (rcore_web.c's EmscriptenTouchCallback) and
               GLFW a click the same way, which is right only while the
               picture fills the box - never under `object-fit`. */
            width: 100%;
            height: 100%;
            outline: none;
            /* The builder paints by dragging, so the browser must not claim
               drags for scrolling or pinch-zoom. */
            touch-action: none;
            -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
            -webkit-user-select: none;
            -moz-user-select: none;
            user-select: none;
            image-rendering: pixelated;
          }

          /* Immersive mode. `requestFullscreen` covers desktop, Android and
             iPadOS; Safari on iPhone has no element Fullscreen API at all,
             so the same button falls back to this class, which reclaims
             everything except the browser's own chrome. */
          &.immersive {
            position: fixed;
            /* The part of the viewport that is on screen, as fullscreen.ts
               reads it off `window.visualViewport` - not `inset: 0`. A
               phone lays a fixed box out in the *layout* viewport, which
               is the largest one, the browser's bars collapsed; while a
               bar shows it covers a strip of an `inset: 0` box, and the
               canvas filling that box loses its top or bottom under the
               bar. Without the API the box is the layout viewport. */
            top: var(--vv-top, 0);
            left: var(--vv-left, 0);
            width: var(--vv-width, 100%);
            height: var(--vv-height, 100%);
            z-index: 100;
          }

          /* Immersive mode and real full screen, where the .game element
             is the fullscreen root, lay the stage out the same way: the
             box is the whole viewport, and the stage fills what is left
             inside the notch and home-indicator bands (`viewport-fit=cover`
             in the head), kept as padding. `border-box`, because the
             padding has to come out of the box, not be added to it: under
             content-box sizing the two side bands would widen the box past
             the viewport and push the stage right by the left band - 47 px
             on a landscape iPhone, enough to put the canvas's right edge
             under the browser's own toolbar. */
          &.immersive, &:fullscreen {
            box-sizing: border-box;
            padding: env(safe-area-inset-top) env(safe-area-inset-right) env(safe-area-inset-bottom) env(safe-area-inset-left);
            justify-content: center;
            background: #151515;

            .stage {
              height: 100%;
            }

            .instructions, .tuning {
              display: none;
            }
          }

          .fullscreen-toggle {
            padding: 3px 9px;
            border-radius: 3px;
            border: 0;
            background: rgba(46, 46, 46, 0.75);
            color: #ddd;
            font-family: sans-serif;
            font-size: $font-size;
            cursor: pointer;

            &:hover, &:focus-visible {
              color: #fff;
              background: rgba(46, 46, 46, 0.95);
            }
          }

          .instructions {
            text-align: center;
            font-size: $font-size;
            padding: 8px 12px;
            margin-top: 10px !important;

            p {
              margin: 0.3em 0;
            }
          }
        }

        .footer {
          p {
            margin: 0.3em 0;
          }
        }
      }

      /* Runtime tuning panel (docs/runtime-tuning-design.md). Only shown
         when the loaded wasm exports the dev-tools C API (bb_*), i.e. a
         `just build-web-dev` / PR-preview build - production never has it. */
      .tuning {
        width: min(100vw, 1280px);
        box-sizing: border-box;
        margin-top: 12px;
        padding: 0 12px 12px;
        font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
        font-size: 11px;
        color: #c6c6c6;
        border: 1px solid #444;
        border-radius: 4px;
        background: #262626;

        summary {
          cursor: pointer;
          padding: 8px 0;
          font-family: sans-serif;
          font-size: $font-size;
          user-select: none;

          .badge {
            display: inline-block;
            margin-left: 6px;
            padding: 1px 6px;
            border-radius: 3px;
            background: #5a3d0c;
            color: #f5c76a;
            font-size: 9px;
            letter-spacing: 0.05em;
            text-transform: uppercase;
          }
        }

        .toolbar {
          display: flex;
          flex-wrap: wrap;
          gap: 6px;
          align-items: center;
          margin-bottom: 8px;

          input[type="search"] {
            flex: 1 1 160px;
            min-width: 120px;
          }
        }

        .tabs {
          display: flex;
          flex-wrap: wrap;
          gap: 4px;
          margin-bottom: 8px;

          button[aria-selected="true"] {
            background: #4a4a4a;
            color: #fff;
          }
        }

        button, input[type="search"], textarea {
          font: inherit;
          color: #ddd;
          background: #333;
          border: 1px solid #555;
          border-radius: 3px;
          padding: 3px 8px;
        }

        button {
          cursor: pointer;
        }

        button:hover {
          background: #3e3e3e;
        }

        button.reset {
          padding: 1px 5px;
          color: #999;
        }

        .status {
          margin-left: auto;
          color: #8fbf8f;
          white-space: nowrap;
          overflow: hidden;
          text-overflow: ellipsis;
          max-width: 40%;
        }

        .status.error {
          color: #e88;
        }

        .scroll {
          overflow-x: auto;
        }

        table {
          border-collapse: collapse;
          width: 100%;
          margin-bottom: 10px;

          th, td {
            padding: 2px 6px;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #383838;
            text-align: left;
            white-space: nowrap;
            vertical-align: middle;
          }

          th {
            color: #999;
            font-weight: normal;
          }

          td.name {
            color: #e0e0e0;
            cursor: help;
          }

          td.name.changed {
            color: #f5c76a;
          }

          td.ctl {
            width: 260px;
          }

          td.val {
            width: 80px;
            text-align: right;
            font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
          }

          td.def {
            width: 70px;
            text-align: right;
            color: #777;
            font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
          }

          td.badge span {
            padding: 0 5px;
            border-radius: 3px;
            background: #3b3b3b;
            color: #aaa;
            font-size: 9px;
            text-transform: uppercase;
          }

          input[type="range"] {
            width: 160px;
            vertical-align: middle;
          }

          input[type="number"] {
            width: 84px;
            font: inherit;
            color: #ddd;
            background: #333;
            border: 1px solid #555;
            border-radius: 3px;
            padding: 1px 4px;
            text-align: right;
          }

          input[type="number"].changed {
            color: #f5c76a;
          }
        }

        h4 {
          margin: 6px 0 4px;
          font-weight: normal;
          color: #999;
        }

        .import {
          display: none;
          gap: 6px;
          margin: 0 0 8px;

          &.open {
            display: flex;
          }

          textarea {
            flex: 1;
            min-height: 60px;
          }
        }
      }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrapper">
    <div class="game">
        <div class="stage">
            <canvas id="canvas" tabindex="-1"></canvas>
            <div class="overlay-controls">
                <button class="fullscreen-toggle" id="fullscreen-toggle" type="button"
                        title="Play full screen" data-i18n="fullscreen" data-i18n-title="fullscreenTitle">&#9974; Full screen
                </button>
                <a class="subscribe-link" href="/subscribe" data-i18n="subscribe">Subscribe for updates.</a>
            </div>
            <div class="loading" id="loading" role="status" aria-live="polite">
                <p class="loading-title" data-i18n="loading">Loading&hellip;</p>
                <div class="loading-track">
                    <div class="loading-bar" id="loading-bar"></div>
                </div>
                <p class="loading-note" id="loading-note" data-i18n="fetching">Fetching the game</p>
            </div>
            <p class="turn" data-i18n="turn">Turn your phone sideways to play.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="instructions">
            <!-- The words are src/scripts/strings.ts's, in the language the
                 game will speak; the English here is what a page with no
                 script shows. -->
            <p data-i18n="keysOne">Arrows to drive, <kbd>Space</kbd> to fire, <kbd>r</kbd> to restart.</p>
            <p data-i18n="keysTwo">Two players: Arrows + <kbd>Space</kbd> for player 1, <kbd>W</kbd><kbd>A</kbd><kbd>S</kbd><kbd>D</kbd> +
                <kbd>Left Shift</kbd> for player 2.</p>
        </div>
        <details class="tuning" id="tuning" hidden>
            <summary>Tuning <span class="badge">dev build</span></summary>
            <div class="toolbar">
                <input type="search" id="tun-filter" placeholder="filter knobs…" autocomplete="off"/>
                <button id="tun-restart"
                        title="Restart the round (same as R) so a tuned set plays out from a fresh spawn">Restart round
                </button>
                <button id="tun-reset" title="Every knob back to its default">Reset all</button>
                <button id="tun-copy-json"
                        title="Copy only the knobs that differ from default, as JSON (paste into --tuning file or Import)">
                    Copy JSON
                </button>
                <button id="tun-import" title="Paste a JSON patch to apply">Import…</button>
                <button id="tun-copy-rust" title="Copy the changed knobs as tunables! rows for src/tuning.rs">Copy as
                    Rust
                </button>
                <span class="status" id="tun-status"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="import" id="tun-import-box">
                <textarea id="tun-import-text" placeholder='{"tank_speed": 300, "wall_max_health.wood": 50}'></textarea>
                <button id="tun-import-apply">Apply</button>
            </div>
            <nav class="tabs" id="tun-tabs"></nav>
            <div class="scroll" id="tun-body"></div>
        </details>
    </div>
    <div class="footer">
        <div>
            <p data-i18n="feedback">Feedback and suggestions are welcome via <a href="https://github.com/otobrglez">@otobrglez</a>. </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<script src="../scripts/main.ts"></script>
<script is:inline defer src="/game/bongbong.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
